# Module boundaries

If a cohesive group of classes is actively used by other classes (other layers/features), extract that group into a separate Gradle module.

## Criteria

- Cohesive group (package/subsystem), not a single utility class
- Consumed by ≥2 other layers/features, or clearly shared from day one (e.g. design-system)
- Module boundary = public API; internals stay internal
- Do not split “just in case”: if only one feature uses the group, keep it in that module

## Examples in this repo

- tokens + base UI → `:design-system` (consumes shared `design-theme` artifact)
- nav models → package in `:shared` until a second consumer needs a dedicated module
